content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104 standby unit, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction back pull-out pump, filtered-water line (chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite). Serial plate painted over and unreadable.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft seal leaking steadily. The manual lists 'Leakage at shaft seal' as a fault symptom whose corrective action is to replace the mechanical seal (5.2) and check alignment (5.4). The evidence gives no leak-rate limit, so the defect justifies a planned seal replacement. It does not on its own trigger a documented stop.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 3.0 mm/s against Figure 3 of the HF-300 manual: 3.0 mm/s is above the Zone A/B boundary (2.8) and below the Zone B/C boundary (4.5). That puts it in Zone B, 'Long-term operation'. It is not in Zone C (4.5-7.1, plan maintenance) or Zone D (>7.1, stop the pump). The report does not say whether this was RMS or which bearing housing was measured. Figure 3 applies to the highest reading from both housings.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature 69 C against the manual specification for bearing housing temperature (normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C): 69 C is within the normal band but only 1 C below its upper limit. It is 11 C below alarm and 21 C below trip. Temperature is measured on the housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No reading reaches a documented stop limit (no Zone D vibration, no 90 C trip temperature). The seal leak should be repaired as a planned job. The pump is a standby unit, so take it out of standby availability and isolate it for the repair rather than run it.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical seal faces. This is the first listed cause of leakage at the shaft seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the pump is serial HF3-22000 or above and still has the original HF3-450 component seal: early seal failure caused by a revised sleeve tolerance, per SB-2026-014. This cannot be confirmed until the serial is known.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal run dry. The seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge and the seal must never run dry. A standby unit may have been started without being properly filled or vented.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. This is listed as a cause of seal leakage, high vibration and high bearing temperature. Vibration (Zone B) and temperature (69 C, near the 70 C normal limit) are both elevated but within limits, which is consistent with possible misalignment but does not confirm it.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Establish the pump serial number before ordering or fitting the seal. Carefully remove the paint from the serial plate, or obtain the serial from asset or purchase records. Serial HF3-22000 and above: use cartridge seal HF3-450B with 30 Nm gland torque per SB-2026-014. Below HF3-22000: use HF3-450 and manual Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the pump from standby duty. Isolate and drain the pump. The pumped fluid is sodium hypochlorite-dosed filtered water.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg) using lifting equipment. The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the seal and shaft sleeve and inspect the sleeve for scoring. On pumps serial HF3-22000 and above, replace sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Record the seal face condition, and any evidence of dry running, to confirm the cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the new mechanical seal (HF3-450B or HF3-450 according to serial) and a new casing gasket HF3-120. The gasket must be replaced whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten all fasteners on lightly oiled threads: casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm; impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm; bearing housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm, if disturbed. Tighten the seal gland nuts M10 to 30 Nm if HF3-450B is fitted (serial HF3-22000 and above), or to 25 Nm if HF3-450 is fitted (below HF3-22000).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Carry out laser shaft alignment, because the bearing housing and rotating assembly have been moved. Tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm; angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to standby, fill and vent the casing and confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from discharge is in place. The seal must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading against Figure 3; the target is Zone A/B, at or below 4.5 mm/s. Check housing temperature against the 70 C normal limit. If temperature stays near or above 70 C or vibration rises, check grease quantity and inspect the bearings (replace as a pair per 5.3 if worn).",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, pre-set. Fit ONLY if serial is HF3-22000 or above (supersedes HF3-450 per SB-2026-014).",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Mechanical seal, component type. Fit ONLY if serial is below HF3-22000.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever the casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Contingency spare, fit if inspection shows scoring (replace if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth on serial HF3-22000 and above).",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before starting work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The filtered-water line pumps P-101 to P-106 are chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Treat drained fluid and seal leakage as chemically contaminated and control exposure accordingly.",
      "citations": [
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg. Lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. Confirm the casing is full and the Plan 11 seal flush is working before any test run.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair, 6.0 h, 2 technicians) is not planned. Readings are within limits; add it only if inspection or post-repair checks show bearing wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part number: the manual parts list (AQ-OM-300 Rev D) specifies HF3-450 component seal. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes it with cartridge seal HF3-450B, but only for HF-300 serial HF3-22000 and above. Pumps below HF3-22000 continue to use HF3-450. The P-104 serial plate is unreadable, so which document applies cannot yet be decided. The serial must be confirmed before the seal is selected.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm (M10). SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B on serial HF3-22000 and above. Use 30 Nm only if HF3-450B is fitted on a qualifying serial. Otherwise use 25 Nm per Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve inspection: manual 5.2 requires inspecting the sleeve for scoring. SB-2026-014 says HF3-450B is pre-set with no sleeve measurement needed, but still requires sleeve replacement if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm. Apply the 0.1 mm criterion on serial HF3-22000 and above. The manual gives no numeric scoring limit for older pumps.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is the P-104 serial number (and build date)? It determines whether SB-2026-014 applies (HF3-450B, 30 Nm) or the manual (HF3-450, 25 Nm). Asset or purchase records, or careful paint removal from the plate, are needed.",
    "Was the 3.0 mm/s vibration measured as RMS velocity, on which bearing housing, and while the standby pump was running? Figure 3 requires the highest reading from both housings.",
    "Which bearing housing does the 69 C reading come from, and was it taken under running conditions?",
    "What PPE and handling controls does site procedure require for sodium hypochlorite-dosed water? The evidence only states that the line is dosed.",
    "Is HF3-450B approved for use on pumps below serial HF3-22000? The bulletin does not say.",
    "What sleeve scoring limit applies to pumps below serial HF3-22000 using HF3-450? The manual only says to inspect for scoring.",
    "Is there a documented acceptable seal leak rate or a leak-based stop criterion? None is given in the evidence.",
    "How was the standby unit operated before the leak? Records are needed to confirm or rule out dry running as the cause."
  ]
}
